WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.580
How Mossville got its name?

2
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:16.540
Back in the day, Jim . . . Jim Moss was my uncle.

3
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:21.840
He was my grandfather's brother, which was Henry Moss.

4
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:37.480
Jim Moss had the post office and my grandfather, Henry Moss, had a little grocery store.

5
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:46.480
And that's how Mossville got its name, Jim Moss.

6
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.640
I mean, from my uncle and my grandfather, Mossville.

7
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.620
My mother said when she was twelve years old, she used to work in that little store.

8
00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.400
She’d leave school and come by and work in the store in the evening, you know.

9
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.140
So that's how I knew about the store.

10
00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:11.900
So when I was about ten years old my mother and my stepdad built a place, Sweet Dream Parlor.

11
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.980
My mother would tell me that's how Mossville got its name.

12
00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:19.500
See I was . . . like, I probably wasn't born then I don't guess.

13
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.360
Maybe I was a baby.

14
00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.820
I don't know, but Uncle Jim had the post office.

15
00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.600
My grandfather, my momma's daddy, he had the grocery store.

16
00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:34.860
That's how Mossville got the name Mossville.

17
00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.960
So they have so many different stories about that.

18
00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:39.340
They never recognized my grandfather.

19
00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:50.920
McKeever Edwards, Sr. never recognized him about the . . . how Mossville got its name.

20
00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:54.120
But that's how Mossville got the name.

21
00:01:54.120 --> 00:02:02.960
On that paper here where it says where my . . . about the slaves in Mossville over here, it says Henry Moss.

22
00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.460
That was my grandfather.

23
00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:08.640
That was Momma's daddy.

24
00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:15.960
Back in the day, they used to tell me all the time that Indians [Native Americans] lived in Mossville.

25
00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:22.440
And where one of those house was, he would take me over there and he would show me, they had the little humps in the ground.

26
00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:26.040
That was their burial ground, the Indians.

27
00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:36.020
Because my grandmother was an Indian and her brother Uncle [Sanky?] or Uncle Henry.

28
00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:41.160
Indians lived out there back in the day.

29
00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.320
My mother always told me that.
